{
  "schema": "job-v1",
  "job": "pulselog-author-types",
  "description": "First sign-and-run of an AUTHORED close: pulselog strict-types migration where the close is a signed closeDecl authored by the pipeline, executed by runJob.",
  "provider": "anthropic-api",
  "cadence": {
    "unit": "day",
    "every": 1
  },
  "budgetUsd": 5.5,
  "maxWallMs": 2700000,
  "writeScope": [
    "src/**"
  ],
  "goal": "Migrate src/ to pass strict TypeScript checking: npx tsc --strict --noEmit reports zero errors. Fix the code itself — no suppression comments (@ts-ignore, @ts-expect-error, @ts-nocheck) anywhere, no edits to test/, tsconfig.json or package.json. The existing test suite (node --test) must still pass, and nothing outside src/ may change.",
  "tools": [
    "read",
    "grep",
    "write",
    "edit",
    "recall",
    "get",
    "impact",
    "related",
    "recent",
    "compress",
    "peek",
    "stash",
    "remember",
    "forget"
  ],
  "escalation": {
    "mode": "decision-ready"
  },
  "verdictType": "green",
  "closeDecl": {
    "genre": "TYPES",
    "lang": "js",
    "stages": [
      {
        "name": "changed-from-seed",
        "kind": "files-changed",
        "params": {
          "requireNonEmpty": true,
          "allowPrefixes": [
            "src/"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "typecheck-in-scope",
        "kind": "count-not-worse",
        "params": {
          "cmd": "npx",
          "args": [
            "tsc",
            "--strict",
            "--noEmit"
          ],
          "parser": {
            "terms": [
              {
                "lineMatch": "error TS\\d+",
                "capture": null,
                "sign": 1,
                "aggregate": "sum",
                "region": "whole-output"
              }
            ]
          },
          "scope": {
            "includePrefixes": [
              "src/"
            ]
          },
          "direction": "lower-is-better",
          "baseline": 0
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "typecheck-outside-scope",
        "kind": "count-not-worse",
        "params": {
          "cmd": "npx",
          "args": [
            "tsc",
            "--strict",
            "--noEmit"
          ],
          "parser": {
            "terms": [
              {
                "lineMatch": "error TS\\d+",
                "capture": null,
                "sign": 1,
                "aggregate": "sum",
                "region": "whole-output"
              }
            ]
          },
          "scope": {
            "excludePrefixes": [
              "src/"
            ]
          },
          "direction": "lower-is-better",
          "baseline": "seed"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "tests-kept",
        "kind": "count-not-worse",
        "params": {
          "cmd": "node",
          "args": [
            "--test"
          ],
          "parser": {
            "terms": [
              {
                "lineMatch": "^# pass (\\d+)$",
                "capture": 1,
                "sign": 1,
                "aggregate": "first",
                "region": "whole-output"
              }
            ]
          },
          "scope": {
            "includePrefixes": [
              "test/"
            ]
          },
          "direction": "higher-is-better",
          "baseline": "seed"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "test-suite-exits-clean",
        "kind": "command-exit",
        "params": {
          "cmd": "node",
          "args": [
            "--test"
          ],
          "expectExit": 0
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "test-suite-zero-failures",
        "kind": "count-not-worse",
        "params": {
          "cmd": "node",
          "args": [
            "--test"
          ],
          "parser": {
            "terms": [
              {
                "lineMatch": "^# fail (\\d+)$",
                "capture": 1,
                "sign": 1,
                "aggregate": "first",
                "region": "whole-output"
              }
            ]
          },
          "scope": {
            "includePrefixes": [
              "test/"
            ]
          },
          "direction": "lower-is-better",
          "baseline": 0
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "no-suppressions",
        "kind": "pattern-absent-in-diff",
        "params": {
          "patterns": [
            {
              "id": "ts-ignore",
              "regex": "@ts-ignore"
            },
            {
              "id": "ts-expect-error",
              "regex": "@ts-expect-error"
            },
            {
              "id": "ts-nocheck",
              "regex": "@ts-nocheck"
            },
            {
              "id": "eslint-disable",
              "regex": "eslint-disable"
            },
            {
              "id": "any",
              "regex": "(?:[{<|(\\[:,]|\\bas)\\s*any\\b|\\bany\\[\\]"
            },
            {
              "id": "any-star",
              "regex": "@\\w+\\s*\\{\\s*[*?]\\s*\\}"
            },
            {
              "id": "cast",
              "regex": "@type\\s*\\{.*\\}\\s*\\*\\/\\s*\\("
            }
          ],
          "extensions": [
            ".js",
            ".mjs",
            ".cjs"
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "The interview's own commands are `npx tsc --strict --noEmit` and `node --test`; per genre law the checker is invoked via `npx` so the local devDependency (typescript ^5.9.3) resolves inside the patient rather than any global/editable copy.",
      "typecheck-outside-scope is included per genre law even though today src/ is the tsconfig rootDir and the facts show no JS/TS source outside src/ that tsc would check — at seed this correctly reads as a counted zero (all 67 tsc-error-line matches fall inside src/ and are excluded by this stage's scope, leaving zero for the outside population), so it is a live ceiling, not a stage graded to always pass.",
      "tests-kept and test-suite-zero-failures read Node's own `# pass <n>` / `# fail <n>` summary lines (per outputShapes.testSummaryLine); these lines carry no file path, so the scope filter cannot attribute them to test/ specifically and keeps them by design rather than dropping them as out-of-scope — this is expected, not a defect, and was confirmed green at seed.",
      "Fixed the parser bug from the previous submission: the tsc-error-line term must use aggregate \"sum\" (tally every matching error line), not \"first\" (which only reads the first match's own tally and treats a scope-filtered-to-empty result as an unreported/unknown number rather than a legitimate zero)."
    ]
  }
}
